<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Spanish Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1701">1701</a>–<a href="/years/1714">1714</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Spanish Succession was a European conflict fought from 1701 to 1714 over who should inherit the Spanish throne after the death of the childless Charles II. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> claimant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip of Anjou</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> backed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> candidate. Philip V kept the throne, but under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht">Treaty of Utrecht</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> lost its European possessions, a key stage in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Spanish Succession" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DavidDijkgraaf · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Final_War_of_the_Spanish_Succession_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
